DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerChabot StaffDoors 7:00PM\, Mov
 ie 7:30PM\nIt’s Sci-Fi Night at Chabot! Bring a friend and come up to Ch
 abot for a one-night-only screening of the original Dune in our state-of-t
 he-art 70-foot Planetarium dome! Come early to enjoy light bites & themed 
 cocktails in this fun\, after-hours date night under the stars. Plus\, che
 ck out our NASA Ames Visitor Center and AstroLight exhibit\, open late jus
 t for this event!\nPlanetarium seating is limited. Once filled\, we will o
 pen ticket sales for a second showing in our Theater location\, located ac
 ross from the Planetarium\, on the first floor. If you are planning to att
 end a Sci-Fi Night event with a group and you would like to sit together\,
  please ensure that all tickets booked are for the same location.\nPlease 
 note that this event takes place in the Spees building only. The Dellums b
 uilding\, including the Co-Lab exhibit hall\, will be closed to the public
 \, with the Observation Deck accessible from the outside Deck gate from 7:
 30pm – 10:30pm for Free Public Telescope Viewing.\n\n$20.00\n\nTickets: 
 https://chabotspace.org/calendar/sci-fi-night-dune-1984/\nDetails: https:/
 /sf.funcheap.com/scifi-night-dune-1984/\nSource: Funcheap SF
