BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film: Defiant to the Last- Resistance at the Tule Lake Jail
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T210000
DTSTAMP:20261111T063824Z
UID:funcheap-1646534@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Movies
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerDefiant to the Last filmFilm S
 creening & Discussion of Defiant to the Last\, Resistance at the Tule Lake
  Jail\nwith Filmmaker Emiko Omori and\nSatsuki Ina\, author of The Poet an
 d the Silk Girl\nAbout the Film from the Defiant to the Last website:\n“
 Based on lies and wartime propaganda\, during WWII the U.S. government for
 cibly removed and incarcerated more than 125\,000 innocent Japanese Americ
 ans in ten American concentration camps\, solely because of their race.\n
 “At all the prison sites\, despite the mythology of quiet compliance\, J
 apanese Americans showed moral courage\, resisted\, and refused to accept 
 the government’s abuse. Defiant to the Last tells the story of the Tule 
 Lake Segregation Center where dissident Japanese Americans were demonized 
 and punished for speaking out against the false wartime incarceration.”\
 nRevolution Books is showing this film because the story of resistance to 
 the unjust treatment of the Japanese Americans in WW II resonates deeply w
 ith our own time\, when immigrants’ rights are stripped away\, they are 
 demonized\, and some deported to torture prisons in countries they’ve ne
 ver lived in – and people who oppose this treatment are attacked and vil
 ified by the government.\nThis is a time for defiance\, for voices of cons
 cience to speak out\, and for revolution. Defiant to the Last brings cruci
 al experience and important lessons from the past\, and we are very glad t
 o be able to bring Satsuki Ina and Emiko Omori to our store.\nWatch th...\
 n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://revolutionbooks.org\nDetails: https://sf.funch
 eap.com/film-defiant-resistance-tule-lake-jail/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/defian
 ttothelastposter1.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261111T063824Z
LOCATION:Revolution Books\, 2444 Durant Avenue Berkeley\, CA 94704
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/film-defiant-resistance-tule-lake-jail/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“Secret Cinema Society” David Lynch Films + Drag Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T003000
DTSTAMP:20261117T035757Z
UID:funcheap-1647582@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Movies
DESCRIPTION:Enter the strange\, surreal & wonderfully unsettling world of 
 David Lynch ft Blue Velvet and Mulhollald Drive + a special drag performan
 ce\n\nSecret Cinema Society invites you to escape the ordinary and immerse
  yourself in Lynch’s unmistakable universe of mystery\, suspense\, and s
 urreal storytelling. The evening kicks off with an hour of themed specialt
 y drinks\, setting the mood for a night of cinematic intrigue. Mingle with
  fellow film lovers\, connect with like-minded cinephiles\, and soak up th
 e atmosphere before settling in for a double feature of two unforgettable 
 films: Blue Velvet and Mulholland Drive.\nBut the night doesn’t end when
  the first credits roll. During intermission\, enjoy a special drag perfor
 mance inspired by the eccentric\, theatrical\, and wonderfully bizarre spi
 rit of David Lynch’s cinematic universe. Expect unexpected glamour\, cap
 tivating entertainment\, and a little dose of the surreal before returning
  to the big screen.\n\nWhether you’re a longtime Lynch devotee or discov
 ering his work for the first time\, join us for an evening of cult cinema\
 , live performance\, and good company.\nTwo films. One drag performance. A
  night of beautiful strangeness. Welcome to Secret Cinema Society.\nThis i
 s a fundraiser for Art for Civil Discourse – a new non-profit dedicated 
 to providing an affordable community space for local artists.\nmore info a
 t: https://www.discoursesf.com/\n\n$15.00\n\nTickets: https://www.eventbri
 te.com/e/secret-cinema-society-ft-david-lynch-drag-show-tickets-2004409754
 533?aff=oddtdtcreator&amp\;keep_tld=true\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com
 /secret-cinema-society-david-lynch-films-drag-show-sf/\nSource: Funcheap S
 F
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/David-
 Lynch-event-brite-2.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261117T035757Z
LOCATION:Discourse SF\, 275 8th Street San Francisco 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/secret-cinema-society-david-lynch-films-drag-s
 how-sf/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Aliens (Special Edition)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T204500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T224500
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17923121@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Where its predecessor was a slow-burn suspenser\, Cameron’s 
 ALIENS is a bombastic\, no-holds-barred exosuit fight to the finish\, an e
 xpress elevator to hell\, goin’ down! Lone survivor Ripley (Sigourney We
 aver) goes back for a rematch with the creatures who slaughtered the crew 
 of the Nostromo\, this time bringing along a squad of hard-boiled space ma
 rines whose number includes the great Bill Paxton\, Jenette Goldstein\, an
 d Lance Henriksen’s mumblety-peg-playing android Bishop. Rounding out th
 e superb supporting players are the aliens themselves\, pinnacles of pre-C
 GI visual effects that just keep coming\, and coming\, and coming\, and co
 ming… while Mead’s contributions can mostly be seen in the blade-like 
 military vessel Sulaco and the unforgettable “Power Loader” donned by 
 Ripley for the main event grudge match.\n\nScreening in Cameron’s prefer
 red cut\, which adds nearly 20 minutes of material not seen in the theatri
 cal version\, including glimpses of life at the ill-fated Hadley’s Hope 
 colony and some “kickass” motion-activated turret guns.\n\n“Hot off 
 of the immediate successes of Blade Runner and TRON\, Syd Mead was enliste
 d by Cameron to build out the world of ALIENS\, his muscular\, action-orie
 nted second chapter to Ridley Scott’s now-iconic 1979 masterpiece. The c
 enterpiece of Mead’s designs is the U.S.S. Sulaco\, the military spacesh
 ip that transports the Colonial Marines\, infusing the vessel with a funct
 ional and industrial aesthetic that enhanced the film’s gritty realism.
 ” —Future P...\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase
 /22258?siteToken=4m48btf3yavn7xjk5yxk6nc40c\nDetails: https://dothebay.com
 /events/2026/11/20/aliens-special-edition-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34800079/e4312bef-0067-4306-97a0-5d1d1f94d6db.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/20/aliens-special-edition-tickets
END:VEVENT
