 et/34996220/dbf23b43-8387-42ed-af04-79ff8bd39f93.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261017T204148Z
LOCATION:The Castro\, 429 Castro St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94114
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/1/small-town-gay-bar-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Women on the Verge of a Nervous Breakdown (35mm)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T204000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T224000
DTSTAMP:20261126T170128Z
UID:dothebay-18099334@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Part of IN THE MOOD FOR ALMODÓVAR\, presented in anticipation
  of our upcoming run of BITTER CHRISTMAS.\n\nThis fast-paced celebration o
 f hysteria put Almodóvar on the map by joyfully parading his depthless ob
 session with women – especially the wild ones. Driven to the brink by he
 r married lover\, Pepa (Carmen Maura) cries at work\, lights her bed on fi
 re\, and loads the gazpacho with barbiturates. Her girlfriends don’t far
 e much better in this melodramatic farce that runs at a constant parody-le
 vel soap-operatic pitch. It’s no small coincidence that during filming C
 armen Maura grew so angry with the director she outright refused to speak 
 to him.\n\nMen drive the women of this movie to crisis – a trash collect
 or\, Shiite terrorists\, boyfriends\, Antonio Banderas – and the women f
 ight back as a series of peculiar coincidences tightens the social fabric 
 of Madrid. “I thought this only happened in the movies\,” a cab driver
  tells Pepa after she has him tail another cab. Yeah yeah\, her expression
  says\, but it’s headed somewhere very interesting.\n\nRuntime\n\n1h 28m
 \n\nYear\n\n1988\n\nDirector\n\nPedro Almodóvar\n\nFormat\n\n35mm\n\nCoun
 try\n\nSpain\n\nLanguage\n\nIn Spanish with English subtitles\n\nFirst Sho
 wing\n\nNovember 28\, 2026\n\nCategories\n\nRoxCine\n\nIn the Mood for Alm
 odóvar\n\n\,\n\nFeatured\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/p
 urchase/22660?siteToken=4m48btf3yavn7xjk5yxk6nc40c\nDetails: https://dothe
 bay.com/events/2026/12/1/women-on-the-verge-of-a-nervous-breakdown-35mm-ti
 ckets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35574156/9c8a4566-e771-428b-a355-a860afd144ad.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261126T170128Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/1/women-on-the-verge-of-a-nervous-
 breakdown-35mm-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Santacon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T200000
DTSTAMP:20261126T170128Z
UID:dothebay-18081539@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:In attendance for a special post-film Q&A will be original San
 tas John Law and Rob Schmitt\, as well as other surprise guests.\n\nToday\
 , Santacon is known as perhaps the single most hated event on the planet. 
 A dreaded day in which tens of thousands of drunk idiots dress like Santa 
 and invade countless cities around the world to live out their drunkest an
 d most violent instincts.\n\nBut it began as something else entirely: A pi
 ece of absurdism designed to shock people out of their everyday existence 
 by creating a sense of awe and confusion.\n\nBorn from the San Francisco u
 nderground\, the folks who started Santacon in the ’90s are the same peo
 ple who started Burning Man and who served as the real-life inspiration fo
 r Fight Club and Project Mayhem. And today\, they want nothing to do with 
 their Christmas creation.\n\nJoin us for a special screening of SANTACON\,
  a new documentary from director Seth Porges (Class Action Park). Told wit
 h exclusive access to the event’s original creators and with countless h
 ours of never-before-seen home movies from the 1990s\, you’ll be transpo
 rted back in time to a world of awe\, wonder\, and endless possibility.\n\
 nAll Santas are invited to attend in costume.\n\nRuntime\n\n1h 27m\n\nYear
 \n\n2025\n\nDirector\n\nSeth Porges\n\nFormat\n\nDCP\n\nFirst Showing\n\nD
 ecember 2\, 2026\n\nCategories\n\nFeatured\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.u
 swest.veezi.com/purchase/22605?siteToken=4m48btf3yavn7xjk5yxk6nc40c\nDetai
 ls: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/2/santacon-tickets\nSource: DoTheB
 ay
