BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“Decoder” Film Screening: Analog-Age Anti-Capitalist Riot
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T200000
DTSTAMP:20261118T115305Z
UID:funcheap-1642354@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Movies
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event Organizer© Interzone PicturesIn an ear
 ly cyberpunk version of 1980s Berlin\, audiophile F.M. (played by F.M. Ein
 heit of the legendary German noise band Einstürzende Neubauten) spends hi
 s nights tuned into the peaceful\, unobtrusive Muzak played from nearby H 
 Burger restaurants. But when he discovers that it secretly carries sublimi
 nal messages encouraging mindless consumption\, he teams up with a group o
 f urban pirates (led by Genesis P-Orridge) to spread a musical antidote. I
 ts patrons awakened from their fast-food slumber and on the edge of all-ou
 t anti-capitalist insurrection\, H Burger headquarters decides to dispatch
  a special agent to permanently deal with their F.M. problem.\nInspired by
  a 1970 essay by William S. Burroughs (who also stars in the film) and fea
 turing the music of Soft Cell\, Einstürzende Neubauten\, and The The\, De
 coder doubles as a midnight cult gem and an analog-age riot against the en
 croachment of technology on the autonomy of human desire and perception.\n
 \nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/film-screening-decoder-tic
 kets-2002231307740\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/decoder-film-screenin
 g-analogage-anticapitalist-riot-sf/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Websit
 e-quer4.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261118T115305Z
LOCATION:Goethe-Institut San Francisco\, 657 Howard Street San Francisco\,
  CA 94105
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/decoder-film-screening-analogage-anticapitalis
 t-riot-sf/
END:VEVENT
