BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New People: Filipiñana
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T200000
DTSTAMP:20261126T170128Z
UID:dothebay-18070511@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:All listed screenings take place at NEW PEOPLE CINEMA\, locate
 d at 1746 Post Street in Japantown.\n\nDirector Rafael Manuel in person fo
 r a post screening Q&A.\n\nThe Philippines’ official submission for Best
  International Feature Film at the 99th Academy Awards\n\nPresented by Fil
 iKula\n\nAmid stifling heat and pervasive drought\, Isabel (Jorrybell Agot
 o)\, a 17-year-old Ilokana from the rural north\, works at a posh country 
 club outside Manila\, lining up golf balls for powerful men to drive into 
 the verdant horizon. New to the job\, she wanders the immaculate grounds s
 ampling its luxuries as members\, including an industrialist and his expat
 riate niece\, the club president and his pampered wife\, and a slew of Chi
 nese tourists\, engage in a complex dance with the club’s doting and sub
 servient staff. But something is rotting beneath the pristine fairways of 
 the elite resort\, as Isabel discovers when she tries to return a mislaid 
 golf club to its patriarchal director\, Dr. Palanca (Teroy Guzman). The de
 eper she journeys into its most exclusive corners\, the closer she gets to
  the violent truths of the club\, her native Philippines\, and her own pas
 t..\n\n“A masterwork…with Filipiñana\, Manuel opens new vistas in the
  future of the cinema.” – The New Yorker\n\n“An invigorating dose of
  arch formalism in a sea of mainstream sincerity\, this is the kind of mov
 ie that asks for the viewer’s attention…the angle of a golf club can e
