DESCRIPTION:Winner of the Grand Prix at Cannes\, MINOTAUR is the latest fr
 om Russian filmmaker Andrey Zvyagintsev (LEVIATHAN\, LOVELESS). His riveti
 ng\, razor-sharp tale of personal\, patriarchal\, and governmental corrupt
 ion follows a wealthy CEO who begins to suspect his wife is having an extr
 amarital affair. France’s entry for Best International Feature Film at t
 he 2027 Academy Awards.\n\nNow living in exile\, Russian filmmaker Andrey 
 Zvyagintsev has been creating impeccable\, trenchant allegories about the 
 moral and political condition of his home country throughout the 21st cent
 ury\, and his latest is one of his most riveting and razor-sharp. Set in 2
 022 Russia\, Minotaur centers on middle-aged businessman Gleb (Dmitry Mazu
 rov)\, a transport company CEO who lives an ultra-comfortable domestic lif
 e with his wife Galina (Iris Lebedeva) and teenage son in a sleek modernis
 t home in a private wooded area. As the film begins\, he is tasked by the 
 town’s powerful mayor with drafting a quota of his employees to send to 
 the newly ongoing war in Ukraine\; at the same time\, he begins to suspect
  that Galina is having an affair\, which leads him to take drastic action.
  With the finesse of his stated inspiration Claude Chabrol\, Zvyagintsev h
 as constructed a tale of corruption—personal\, patriarchal\, and governm
 ental—that slow-burns with rage and fearless dark humor.\n\nNominated fo
 r three 2026 Gotham Film Awards\, including Best Director\, Best Internati
 onal Feature\, and Best Adapted Screenplay.\n\n“Beautifully sinist...\n\
 nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/22690?siteToken=4m48
 btf3yavn7xjk5yxk6nc40c\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/10/mi
 notaur-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
