 o\n\nMOViES FOR MANiACS is thrilled to return to The Castro on April 9\, 2
 026. Curated and hosted by Jesse Hawthorne Ficks\, this film series has ce
 lebrated underrated and overlooked films on Bay Area screens for 25 years.
  These once-in-a-lifetime cinematic experiences (often showcasing the film
 makers in person) remind you that “going to the movies” is a magical e
 xperience. Mark your calendar and tell your friends — MOViES FOR MANiACS
  has a slew of cult classics and special guests on the horizon.\n\nBring t
 he whole family to celebrate the 15th Anniversary of Gore Verbinski’s me
 ta-existential masterpiece\, Rango (2011) with the acclaimed writer/direct
 or IN PERSON! The evening will consist of a pre-screening autograph signin
 g followed by a post-screening on-stage Q&A with one of the most unhinged 
 studio directors of the 21st Century.\n\nIt’s time to revisit Rango (201
 1)\, a subversively surreal kids flick that follows a suburban-raised liza
 rd who is suddenly flung into the “”Wild West”” of the Mojave Dese
 rt and is forced to take action as the sheriff of a little town named “
 ”Dirt””. This Oscar winning Animated Feature showcases dozens of uni
 que critters\, and is enhanced by mesmerizing Visual Effects by Industrial
  Light & Magic (ILM). Add to that the gorgeous camera work of Roger Deakin
 s\, o...\n\nAll Ages\nMOViES FOR MANiACS and Another Planet Entertainment 
